# Keep the build context small and the image honest.
#
# .venv matters most: it is a few hundred megabytes of Windows binaries that would be
# useless in a Linux image and, while metas-unclib was still a dependency, would have
# carried a licensed library into the build context. .gitignore already keeps it out of
# git, so a hosting provider building from the repository never sees it; this is what
# keeps a local `docker build` equally clean.

.git
.gitattributes
.github

.venv
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info

# Generated and working directories, both already gitignored.
out
temp

tools/node_modules
tools/package*.json

# Not part of the running application. PLAN.md is a build journal and firstPrompt.md is
# the prompt that started the project; ARCHITECTURE.md is left in because a later change
# set serves it from the site.
PLAN.md
firstPrompt.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
render.yaml
